The login page hands the session token to an application on the person's own computer, such as a command-line tool, with the same contract as `volto-authomatic`: `/login?return_url=<loopback URL>&state=<state>`, then a form POST of `token` and `state` to that URL. A new `/login-handoff` page asks the person first, after any way of signing in and also when they arrive already signed in. Only `http` URLs on `127.0.0.1`, `[::1]` or `localhost` with a port are accepted, and only with a `state`. @ericof
